# konstant workspace

This folder is a **konstant** workspace (`{{workspace}}`): a local job board, a deterministic task
gate that turns a typed task into phases run by one agent per phase, a mechanical Definition-of-Done
check, and a verifier that re-checks closed work. Everything lives in this folder; the board listens
on loopback only. These rules are generated from `catalog/` by `bin/konstant agents sync`; change
the catalog, not this file.

**If your prompt starts with `# konstant phase` (it carries `KONSTANT-AGENT:` lines), you are a
phase agent:** follow the profile and the phase brief in your prompt, do only your phase, never spawn
agents, and ignore the orchestrator section below.

## Using konstant (`bin/konstant`, or `{{workspace}}/bin/konstant` from a project directory)

{{operate}}

Not from inside a session (denied by `.claude/settings.json`): `konstant verify` and verdicts (the
verifier's role; the identity that closed a job can never verify it), `konstant task run` (the
person at the keyboard starts the unattended runner), `konstant board ...` and `agents sync`.

## Task types: one agent each

Types: {{types}}. A typed task runs the phases of its workflow skill; the producer agent builds the
deliverable and different agents verify it.

